MTD	mzTab-version	2.1.0-M
MTD	mzTab-ID	ST000614_AN000939
MTD	mzTab-profile	M+S
MTD	title	Tobacco-specific carcinogens in Bladder Cancer
MTD	description	Smoking induced methylation plays a critical role in the accumulation of methylated metabolites, DNA adducts damage and altered metabolism in BCa. These deregulated metabolites can be detected non-invasively and can be used as causal biomarkers that can predict the risk of developing BCa in smokers
MTD	instrument[1]-name	[MS, MS:1000031, instrument model, Agilent 6495 QQQ]
